# Go source must always check out with LF, regardless of a contributor's
# global/repo `core.autocrlf` -- gofmt's canonical output is LF-terminated,
# so a Windows checkout with autocrlf=true (the commonly recommended
# Windows default) silently converts every .go file to CRLF on `git
# checkout`, and `gofmt -l` then flags every single one as "needs
# reformatting" even though the actual code is untouched and correct (see
# docs/TROUBLESHOOTING.md). Forcing eol=lf here means `task backend:vet`
# stays green regardless of whoever's local autocrlf setting.
*.go text eol=lf
go.mod text eol=lf
go.sum text eol=lf
